                "headline": "Wind Advisory issued November 8 at 3:02PM AKST until November 10 at 6:00PM AKST by NWS Fairbanks AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...South-southeast winds 15 to 30 mph with gusts up to 60 mph\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Isabel Pass & Windy Pass.\n\n* WHEN...From midnight Monday Night to 6 PM AKST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially\nfor high profile vehicles.\n\nGusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree limbs could be\nblown down & a few power outages may result.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The wind gusts look to start ramping up late\nMonday night, peaking Tuesday morning, before tapering Tuesday\nafternoon.",
